# Mechanism: wgpu-feature-compatibility

command: python3 -B scripts/check-wgpu-features.py
inputs:
  - .cairn/mechanisms/wgpu-feature-compatibility
  - Cargo.toml
  - Cargo.lock
  - build.rs
  - src
  - crates
  - reactive-tui-macros
  - examples
  - tests
  - scripts
  - manual
  - README.md
requirements:
  - GPU-001

The validator must reject absent opt-in wiring, a nonoptional dependency,
default-enabled graphics, missing native shader/backend features, and an
active default dependency graph containing wgpu. Corrected fixtures pass.
Locked builds and existing consumer tests run on the declared Rust minimum,
with and without the graphics feature. Configuration inspection alone is not
acceptance. This declaration makes no claim that runtime graphics exist yet.
